    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the clear engine of the offense. With an elite score of 83.29, **Gunnar Henderson** draws a favorable matchup against a right-handed arm with a 4.32 xERA; his leadoff positioning combined with a high likelihood of stolen base success against a slow-delivering pitcher makes him our most bankable asset. **Drake Baldwin** (68.17) and **Kyle Tucker** (67.14) also profile as high-floor, high-upside starters. **Kyle Tucker** specifically benefits from an atmospheric edge, as projected wind blowing out adds a 5% boost to his already strong profile, effectively neutralizing the challenge presented by a left-handed opposing starter.\n\nStrategic lineup construction today heavily weights platoon efficiency and situational leverage to bridge our gaps in counting stats. While **Luis Robert Jr.** struggles against right-handed pitching (-15% dynamic platoon adjustment), the team is forced to roll him out due to depth constraints; conversely, **Sam Antonacci** and **Wade Meckler** provide essential upside at the top of the order, leveraging positive SP skill matchups and prime batting spots to hover near the 60-point threshold. **Coby Mayo** represents the most difficult bench decision, effectively left on the pine due to today's starting lineup configuration; his potential is high, but without a confirmed spot in the order, his utility is strictly capped by our efficiency model. We continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung**, who remain sidelined on the IL, while keeping an eye on **Miguel Vargas**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Luis Lara** to ensure we aren't missing late-breaking value from our bench depth.",
